mber/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-16T18:56:00-07:00","id":667719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Derzhuzad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/666572-shadow-lord-of-mordor?p=667071#post667071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think its unthematic but it would not be a 'Gaian' gift. A gift of that nature would most definitely be powered by the Wyrm or by some spirit that has been tainted by the Wyrm itself. It would most certainly taint the user a little more each time the gift is used. There are a few examples of gifts or rites that Gaian shifters use that brings them closer to the Wyrm in this manner. Many Garou would most definitely look on the user with a great amount of disdain for controlling such creatures, some that dabble in the darker arts might appreciate such a skill however.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about that. This is the tribe that has Direct the Storm in their Gift list. Of course, that an Obedience are kind of much more general than something that specifically targets fomori, which would probably be how you'd go about forcing fomori to go against their fellows.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https:/